          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            These are two separate systems that share a brand and a colour and nothing else. No battery, charger or adapter crosses between them, and buying the right tool on the wrong platform is the most expensive mistake in the Ryobi range — made easy by the fact that both sit on the same aisle in the same green packaging.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people the answer is ONE+ first and 40V only when a specific job demands it. ONE+ covers the workshop, the house and light yard work across hundreds of tools on a battery interface unchanged since 1996. Let a real mower, a serious chainsaw or snow clearing be the thing that justifies adding 40V, and when it does, put the other outdoor tools on that platform too so they share the packs.
